**Shared components (`src/app/shared/components/`)**
- `rank-badge/` (new) — the tier-colored badge used everywhere a rank is
  shown.
- `passphrase-gate/` (new) — the full-screen "enter the passphrase" card.

**Access gate specifics** — a single shared passphrase, not per-user
authentication. The build embeds only a SHA-256 hash
(`environment.accessPassphraseHash`); the app hashes what's typed and
compares client-side; a match is cached in `localStorage` keyed by that
hash. Inert (no gate at all) when the hash is empty, which is the default
for local dev. Does **not** gate the Supabase RPCs — those remain reachable
by anyone with the app URL, same as before. See spec section 50 and
`docs/no-auth-deployment.md`.

**Deployment/docs**
- `.github/workflows/deploy-pages.yml` — hashes an optional
  `ACCESS_PASSPHRASE` repo secret into `environment.production.ts`; never
  writes the plaintext anywhere.
- `.env.example` — documents `ACCESS_PASSPHRASE`.
- `docs/no-auth-deployment.md` — new section explaining the gate is not
  authentication and doesn't change the no-auth security model.
- `docs/git-and-supabase-setup.md` — lists all five migrations in order.
- `README.md` — added a "Feature overview" and "Environment variables"
  section (additive only — the pre-existing "Purpose" section was left
  untouched).

**Spec (`table-football-ranked-app-spec-v2.md`, repo copy + Claude Project
doc, kept identical)** — appended sections 48–51 (Demotion Shield
clarification, Seasons, Access Gate, Implementation Status Notes) rather
than rewriting the original numbered sections in place, so the original
spec stays intact as a historical record; forward-pointers were added at
sections 3, 13, 18, 20, 27, 29, and 35 so a reader lands on the addenda.

