## 2026-09-22 — Migration applied directly via the Supabase MCP connector

Pedro connected a Supabase MCP client mid-session. Used it to inspect the
live `TableFootball` project (`vhcxkacfxffzqgctxmng`) directly instead of
reasoning from static file review:

- Confirmed `20260922160000`'s earlier failed run had rolled back
  completely and atomically (all original constraints and the threshold-5,
  bug-fixed `record_match` from `20260922155000` were still intact,
  unchanged) -- the Supabase SQL editor evidently wraps a pasted multi-
  statement script in one implicit transaction, so the mid-script error
  undid the whole thing rather than leaving a partial state.
- Applied the corrected `20260922160000_placement_matches_ten.sql` via
  `apply_migration`. Verified afterward via direct query:
  `players_placement_matches_played_check` and
  `players_placement_complete_check` now both read `10`; the old unnamed
  `players_check` (threshold 5) is gone.
- Confirmed Duarte's row (the player who hit the original 400) is
  untouched and clean: still `4/10` placement matches, no orphaned data
  from the earlier failed attempts.
- Ran the security/performance advisors as a sanity check post-DDL-change.
  Nothing new: the SECURITY warnings are `record_match`/`start_season`
  being anon-executable `SECURITY DEFINER` functions, which is intentional
  per the no-auth model (see `docs/no-auth-deployment.md`); the
  PERFORMANCE notes (a few unindexed match-participant foreign keys, two
  currently-unused indexes) are pre-existing and minor at this data
  volume, not caused by this change.

No further action needed from Pedro -- the fix is live. He can retry
recording Duarte's match in the app.

