## 2026-09-22 — Third bug: players_check3 required every ranked player to always have an active shield

Testing continued after the placement-ten fix: Pedro tried recording
Andre & Diogo vs Duarte & Matheus (Team B won) and got a third 400, this
time `players_check3`:

```
Failing row contains (..., Diogo, ..., Iron II, 65, 10, t, f, f, t, 7, 3, ...)
```

Diogo was finishing his 10th (final) placement match on this exact match
(and losing it). Checked directly against the live database via the
now-connected Supabase MCP client:

```
players_check3: CHECK (((visible_rank = 'Unranked') = (NOT demotion_shield_active)))
```

That `=` is a biconditional, not the one-directional rule section 18
actually specifies. Besides correctly forbidding an Unranked player from
having an active shield, it also forced the reverse: every *ranked* player
had to have `demotion_shield_active = true` at all times, which is never
true in normal play (the shield starts inactive and only arms at a rank
floor). This existed since the very first migration but had never been
exercised -- until the placement-ten fix landed earlier today, no match in
this database's history had ever been recorded for a player who had
already left Unranked; every match so far happened during someone's
placement run.

**Fix:** `supabase/migrations/20260922162000_fix_ranked_demotion_shield_check.sql`
drops the biconditional and replaces it with
`check (not (visible_rank = 'Unranked' and demotion_shield_active))` --
forbidding only the actually-invalid combination. Applied directly to the
live project via the Supabase MCP connector and verified by querying
`pg_constraint` afterward; also written to the repo migration file,
`docs/git-and-supabase-setup.md` (migration 8), and spec addendum section
53.

Pedro can retry recording that match now.
